>>
endobj
164 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 351 0 R
/E (The increase in this battery storage capacity is mainly driven by the efforts of governments around the world to produce more renewable energy. In Europe alone, the most recent study found that in 2024 Europe had 61.1 GWH. The current goal is that by 2030, Europe will have a total 400 gigawatt hours of energy storage capacity. Although, at the minute we do not know what type of batteries will be used, we have seen that batteries which are rich in nickel tend to have a longer life span and also are more energy dense. As a result, we could assume that these battery storage facilities will incorporate a noticeable amount of nickel in their products. Needless to say, this would drastically increase the demand for nickel. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
