167 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 353 0 R
/E (There are reasons to be optimistic about nickel. Firstly, batteries that are primarily made out nickel have proven to have a longer life span and to also be more energy dense. At the moment, nickel is also seen as a cheaper alternative to materials such as cobalt or lithium that are also used in batteries. Secondly, Europe plans to reduce tailpipe emissions from cars by 2035. Why is this important? The replacement for these internal combustion engined cars will most likely be battery electric vehicles which heavily use nickel to create them. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6 7]
>>
endobj
