189 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 369 0 R
/T (Gold often has a low or negative correlation with traditional asset classes such as equities and bonds. This means that during periods of market turbulence, gold prices may remain stable or even increase, providing protection against market downturns. This characteristic underpins its reputation as a safe haven asset within diversified portfolios. )
/E (Gold often has a low or negative correlation with traditional asset classes such as equities and bonds. This means that during periods of market turbulence, gold prices may remain stable or even increase, providing protection against market downturns. This characteristic underpins its reputation as a safe haven asset within diversified portfolios. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
190 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 369 0 R
/T (Empirical evidence supports this view. Figure 3 shows the relationship between gold daily returns and equities \(S&P 500\) daily returns, with a Pearson correlation coefficient of 0.0299. The near-zero correlation indicates that gold moves largely independently of equity markets, reinforcing its role as a diversifier. This weak relationship suggests that gold can help reduce overall portfolio volatility, particularly during periods of market stress. )
/E (Empirical evidence supports this view. Figure 3 shows the relationship between gold daily returns and equities \(S&P 500\) daily returns, with a Pearson correlation coefficient of 0.0299. The near-zero correlation indicates that gold moves largely independently of equity markets, reinforcing its role as a diversifier. This weak relationship suggests that gold can help reduce overall portfolio volatility, particularly during periods of market stress. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
